This file is a summary. The two files it points at hold the actual licence
texts; if they ever disagree with this summary, they win.

Four sets of vendored files carry their own terms, which apply to those files
rather than to this project. Three of them reach a consumer; the fourth never
leaves the documentation site.

  * The typefaces under assets/fonts/ — Noto Sans, Noto Serif, Noto Sans
    Display and Noctua Iosevka under the SIL Open Font License 1.1, and
    Symbols Nerd Font, which Nerd Fonts ships with its MIT license. The icon
    sets Nerd Fonts gathers keep their own upstream licences, and not all of
    them are MIT: Codicons and Font Awesome, for instance, are under CC BY
    4.0. Each licence sits beside the files it covers, and the OFL requires it
    to keep travelling with them. assets/fonts/ATTRIBUTION.md records what is
    here and why, and where each icon set's terms are.

  * The icon drawings under assets/icons/ — Lucide under the ISC license, and
    Octicons under the MIT license, each with its licence in its directory.

  * three.js, under assets/vendor/three/ — MIT.

  * The photographed owl, assets/vendor/owl/owl.glb — CC BY-NC 4.0:
    attribution required, non-commercial only. One example on the
    documentation site loads it. It is copied into no shipped artifact and
    dist/ receives no byte of it, so nothing a consumer installs is encumbered
    by it — and the day anything documented here is sold, it is the first
    thing that has to go. Terms in assets/vendor/owl/ATTRIBUTION.md.
